<title>LITHUANIA: SAVINGS BANK SAYS 7 MO 8.72 MLN LITAS LOSSES.</title>
<headline>SAVINGS BANK SAYS 7 MO 8.72 MLN LITAS LOSSES.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The first seven months of 1997</p>
<p>(all amounts in million of litas unless othervise stated)</p>
<p>    Net losses		  8.719    vs net profit 8.673</p>
<p>    Assets		     1.465 bln vs		1.15 bln</p>
<p>    Loan portfolio	     644     vs		505</p>
<p>    Deposits		   1.265 bln vs		1.03 bln</p>
<p>    Individual deposits    1.058 bln vs		888</p>
<p>Notes: The figures for assets, loan portfolio deposits and</p>
<p>individual deposits are compared to the beginning of 1997.</p>
<p>The 74 percent state-run Lithuania's Savings Bank </p>
<p>said in a statement that it had a 5.9 million litas profit</p>
<p>before special provisions were made in the first seven months</p>
<p>of the year.</p>
<p>The bank posted 10.85 million litas audited losses for the</p>
<p>first half of 1997.</p>
<p>The bank said its net profit for 1996 was 30 million litas.</p>
<p>The stocks of the bank are traded on the A group of the</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse.</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vi 22 35 17</p>
</text>
